      },
      "message": "feat(ui): show an inverted machine axis in the viewport, setup sheet and NC header\n\nThe origin triad keeps its right-handed program-frame arrows and notes an\ninverted axis of the shown setup's machine under its letter (\"Machine X+\nmoves left (inverted axis)\"). The setup sheet gets a MACHINE AXES section,\none line per inverted axis of the setup's own machine. The script's\nmachine global carries invertedAxes, and fanuc.cps / haas.cps (the only\nposts that translate an inverted axis) write \"(MACHINE X+ MOVES LEFT -\nINVERTED AXIS)\" after the program-name line. Standard machines: no new\nline anywhere. One wording table (machine::inverted_motion /\ninverted_axis_line) feeds the triad and the sheet.\n\nFixes #375\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
